Package: rtranscribe
Type: Package
Title: Speech Recognition with 'transcribe.cpp'
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Johannes B.", "Gruber", , "johannes.gruber@gesis.org",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("The transcribe.cpp authors", role = "cph",
           comment = "Bundled 'transcribe.cpp' sources"),
    person("The ggml authors", role = "cph",
           comment = "Bundled 'ggml' sources"),
    person("Rich Geldreich and Tenacious Software LLC", role = "cph",
           comment = "Bundled 'miniz' sources"),
    person("Mozilla Foundation", role = "cph",
           comment = "Bundled 'llamafile' tinyBLAS sources")
  )
Description: Bindings to 'transcribe.cpp', a C++ automatic speech
    recognition library supporting many model families (Whisper, Parakeet,
    Moonshine, Voxtral and others) in the 'GGUF' format. Transcribe audio to
    text with segment-, word- and token-level timestamps, speaker
    diarization, batch processing and incremental streaming. The
    'transcribe.cpp' and 'ggml' sources are bundled and built from source,
    so no separate installation of the library is required.
